                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Stephen B. Bedrick), according to Petitioner (Stephen B. Bedrick), the correct prima facie standard under Batson is whether there is sufficient evidence to permit a judge to draw a reasonable inference of discrimination."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bedrick",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8d4cb97d6b47ec7b95d25c3197863618da3c6cfedafc9965dcf339a3bff5c063",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8d4cb97d6b47-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bedrick, under Title\u202fVII, the facts must be proved by a preponderance of the evidence (\u201cmore likely than not\u201d) and the McDonnell\u202fDouglas formula applies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bedrick",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8d4cb97d6b47ec7b95d25c3197863618da3c6cfedafc9965dcf339a3bff5c063",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8d4cb97d6b47-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bedrick, the trial judge should not speculate beyond the racial\u2011strike evidence; doing so would be extreme and unusual."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Schalit",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8d4cb97d6b47ec7b95d25c3197863618da3c6cfedafc9965dcf339a3bff5c063",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8d4cb97d6b47-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Schalit, if a party refuses to produce requested discovery, the court may draw an adverse inference, apply issue preclusion, or impose a termination sanction."
        }
      ],
